INT. VELVET TIPS NAIL LOUNGE - BACK ROOM - NIGHT

SUPER: "CORPORATE OFFSITE - DAY 3"

INSERT - A LAPTOP SCREEN. Video call software. A red dot blinks: RECORDING.

DONNA (O.S.)
(sitting straight, clearing her throat, adjusting a headset that does not need adjusting)
Hi. Okay. Is it recording? It says recording. Great. This is my statement for the Q3 culture review, and I want to begin by saying I love this company.

DONNA
(smiling very hard)
I love the open floor plan, which is a nail salon. I love that our break room is also the supply closet, and that our wellness program is the free acetone.

DONNA
(laughing, not laughing)
Which is a joke. That is a joke. Please mark it as humor.

DONNA
(picks up a bottle of polish, reads the label, puts it down)
There are two people in this story. Marcy in Accounts and Marty in Facilities. Marcy sends the emails. Marty receives the emails. Except it's reversed, because the system autocorrects them, and for eleven months I have been invoicing Marty's boiler repairs to Marcy's bonus.

DONNA
(leans toward the camera)
And Marcy knows. And Marty knows. And I know that they know. And nobody says anything, because this is a culture of respect.

DONNA
(whispering)
This is the last time they will speak to me as a colleague.

DONNA
(sits back, normal voice, bright)
So here are my concerns. One. The mandatory fun. We have a fun committee. It meets at six a.m. It is not fun. Two. The feedback system, in which you may give anonymous feedback, provided you sign it.

DONNA
(counting on fingers)
Three. The word "synergy" was used forty-one times at Tuesday's all-hands, and I counted because I was told to be present.

DONNA
(a long breath, shoulders dropping, eyes wet and furious)
And four. I have given this place nine years. I have painted forty thousand nails. Nobody has ever once asked me what colour I would choose.

DONNA
(reaches for a bottle at the edge of frame, a deep, ugly green; holds it up)
This one. It is called "Quarterly Growth." I picked it. I would like it on the record that I picked it.

DONNA
(screws the cap off, looks at the camera)
Marcy. Marty. If you are watching this, and I know you are, because the call is on the big screen in the lobby--

DONNA
(freezes; slowly turns her head toward the door; turns back, composed)
Hi. We'll finish this in the all-hands.

DONNA
(reaches for the laptop, hand shaking, cheerful)
Thank you for your time. Please rate this statement out of five.

SUPER: "THIS CALL HAS BEEN RECORDED FOR TRAINING PURPOSES"
